er way is a resize"] [249 5 "// in place when the length is kept or the slice is the tail (queue 210: _pyio's BytesIO writes"] [250 5 "// b[pos:pos+n] at its end, and a copy of the whole buffer for each write made StringIO quadratic)"] [262 5 "// the extended slice deleted (needed == 0, a value of no bytes too): _canresize first, even for no item"] [324 2 "// bytearray_irepeat (queue 249: in place, a resize; pyi made a new bytearray, so b *= n rebound b)"] [496 2 "// bytearray.take_bytes(n=None, /) (3.15, Objects/bytearrayobject.c's bytearray_take_bytes_impl; queue 237): the first n"] [497 2 "// bytes (negative: from the end, None: all) as bytes, the rest left in the bytearray"] [516 21 "// __index__ may have resized it"] [545 2 "// bytes' other methods, on a copy, their results made bytearrays (once bytes.go's are in its dict)"] [573 1 "// byteIndex is a bytearray's index k (negative from the end), CPython's errors."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[71 28] [74 42] [124 26] [159 27] [198 25] [209 26] [215 24] [215 31] [228 26] [235 30] [245 29] [263 28] [268 25] [268 32] [282 24] [282 31] [292 27] [318 42] [344 34] [352 13] [352 24] [374 42] [385 26] [392 26] [399 42] [424 26] [439 30] [449 26] [465 26] [472 26] [486 26] [504 29] [528 27] [540 28] [540 35] [558 25] [575 22]]} (go/file "bytearray.go" :imports [


